{
  "entity1": {
    "rationale": "The baseline race (entityR2A, 60 trials) shows every run ending off_track, with none finishing. Each run had exactly one line-loss event, and max_error sat at 0.061 to 0.063 m, just above the 0.06 m limit. rms_error was 0.023 to 0.026 m, so the controller tracks well inside the array's reach. The failure is sensing: the line leaves the outer sensors before the robot can recover. I accept the Builder's wider array (x = ±0.06 m, 16 mm footprint), which should keep the line in view past the off-track limit. The flatter signal from 0.03 m spacing gives a smaller steering change per metre of offset, so I raise kp from 3.0 to 3.4 to keep the correction authority. kd stays at 0.3 to damp the 0.03 m forward lag, ki stays at 0.05 to avoid windup, and base_speed stays at 1.2 so the telemetry isolates the sensing change. line_loss stays at last_direction, which keeps the robot turning toward the side it last saw the line. The sensor weights keep the same ±2 to ±1 to 0 pattern, so the steering sign is unchanged. Expected result: line_loss_events near 0 and max_error below 0.06 m on more trials, with progress rising on the oval and s-bend. If line_loss_events stays at 1, the cause is controller recovery, not geometry.",
