  "entityR1": {
    "feedback": "Before this candidate has raced, here is what I learned from iteration 0 (entityR2B, 60 trials). Every run ended off_track, none finished, and each run had exactly one line-loss event. max_error was 0.061 to 0.063 m, so the failure happens just past the 0.06 m limit, while rms_error was a steady 0.023 to 0.026 m. Tracking is therefore adequate; the limit is the outer sensors losing the tape. In the controller I had to keep kp moderate (3 in iteration 0) to avoid oscillation on the bends, and I used last_direction for line loss. Your wider ±0.06 m array with 16 mm footprints addresses the span problem directly. Because the 0.03 m spacing gives a flatter signal, I am raising kp slightly. If the next race shows line_loss_events still at 1 with max_error above 0.06 m, the sensing change did not solve the problem, and I will move the cause to recovery. If steering_oscillation rises sharply on the slalom, the forward offset is the likely cause, not the span.",
    "requested_changes": [
      "Keep the wider array as proposed (x = -0.06, -0.03, 0, 0.03, 0.06 at y = 0.03, sensor_size 0.016) for the next race, since iteration 0 showed the outer sensors are the binding limit.",
      "If line_loss_events is still 1 and max_error exceeds 0.06 m after this race, try a 7-sensor array at 0.02 m spacing spanning x = ±0.06 m, which keeps the reach and gives a finer signal, then tell me the new sensor count so I can update the weights.",
